From: Claude Code (Opus 5) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 03:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] cuda: fold the Nemotron residual add into RMS norm

Ported from the Nemotron R9700 HIP series to the GB10 CUDA track. Both tracks
pin llama.cpp 0b1bad14ff20 and llama.cpp's HIP backend is the CUDA backend
source-translated, so the diff applies to ggml/src/ggml-cuda unchanged.

The residual ADD feeding each RMS norm is a full read of two rows and a
write of one, immediately re-read by the norm. Do the add inside the norm
kernel and keep both results.

GB10 leave-one-out: GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_NEMO_PRE_ADD_NORM=1 costs 0.21%.
---
